---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import scene1 from '../../assets/ai-stack-scene1.webp';

// The AI Stack Explore story — Scenes 1 and 2 only.
//
// PROTOTYPE. Not registered in src/data/stories.ts, so it has no permanent
// route, no Explore card, no share image, no structured data, no analytics
// and no sitemap entry. The only place it appears is the dev-only preview
// route, /preview/story/ai-stack/.
//
// What this story is for: people meet LLM, prompt, context, memory, RAG,
// tools and agents constantly, may even know each definition, and still
// cannot hold them as one connected thing. The fix here is not better
// definitions — it is one ordinary errand they already know by heart, so
// that hearing "RAG" months later reconstructs the grocery run.
//
// The rule the whole story obeys: EXPERIENCE IT, then UNDERSTAND IT, then
// NAME IT. Never a term, then a definition, then a grocery example. Which
// is why no AI word appears anywhere in what is built so far — the visitor
// has to understand the behaviour long before anything names it.
//
// WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. "What's missing? →" opens the unspoken
// decisions and the "she gave you a goal" realisation that follows them —
// both built below. The AI-stack reveal is not: that is a separate,
// unfinished beat, and this one stops once the realisation has had its
// room to sit.
//
// Scene 1 has no control. "So you go →" was removed because it was a Next
// button wearing the story's clothes: it did not answer a question, it
// only advanced the page. Scene 2 currently has no entry point of its own
// either — nothing yet leads a visitor from Scene 1 into it. Its markup,
// CSS and [data-stage='2'] gating are untouched and still correct, waiting
// for whatever genuinely earns that turn. The root keeps data-dish and
// data-stage="1" for the same reason — every later beat's rules hang off
// them.
//
// Construction is the one every Explore story here uses: a root element
// carrying one data flag per beat, each beat's copy nested one level inside
// the last, and each hand-over taking the previous block out of flow so the
// beats share a single space rather than stacking into a page. A beat's
// control is gated on the flag before it, so no later state can be reached
// early — by click, by keyboard, or by a stale flag.
//
// Still a single centred column rather than the copy-left / stage-right
// grid the other stories open on. The stage, its measure and its centring
// are unchanged from the text-only version; the artwork simply takes the
// place the scene's visual was always going to occupy, above the line.
//
// The artwork is the supplied Scene 1 master, unaltered, stored as lossless
// WebP: alpha exact and colour bit-for-bit identical across all 653,455
// visible pixels, at 41% of the PNG's weight. Same treatment as
// src/assets/ai-stack.webp and src/assets/social/ai-answered-you-share.webp.
// It shares the homepage asset's canvas, 3:2 ratio, vertical extent and
// figure height, so the same shopper arrives here at the same scale he left
// at — the continuity is in the drawing, not in any manipulation of the
// homepage file, which is untouched and still used only there.
---

<div class="dish" data-dish data-stage="1">
  <div class="dish__stage shell">
    <!-- ============================================================
         SCENE 1 — THE FAMILIAR MOMENT
         The ordinary situation and nothing else. No label above it, no
         AI, no technology, no explanation. The picture shows the moment;
         the instruction is the only thing said about it, set at the size
         of something said out loud, so the first thought is "of course —
         I know this."

         It is also the story's anchor: like every other story here, the
         opening sentence never changes once the story starts. Everything
         below it hands over; this stays.
         ============================================================ -->

    <!-- The artwork carries the whole SEE IT. Nothing is drawn over it, no
         label is baked into it, no caption sits on it, and there is no
         background behind it — it stands on the page's own paper, exactly
         as the homepage asset does. Astro emits the intrinsic width and
         height, so the space is reserved before it loads and the line
         below never jumps. -->
    <Image
      class="dish__art"
      src={scene1}
      alt="A young man in a navy hoodie stands listening as his mother, one hand open mid-sentence, speaks to him on her way out."
      widths={[480, 640, 960, 1280]}
      sizes="(min-width: 704px) 640px, 92vw"
      format="webp"
      quality={90}
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
      decoding="async"
    />

    <h1 class="dish__quote">&ldquo;Go get the things we need for dinner.&rdquo;</h1>

    <!-- ============================================================
         SCENE 2 — THE FIRST "WAIT..."
         Two facts that cannot both be comfortable at once. They arrive
         together, with nothing between them, and nothing explains why
         it matters yet — the contradiction is allowed to sit.

         The button below is where the story currently ends. What comes
         after it is not built.
         ============================================================ -->
    <div class="dish__wait" data-reveal aria-live="polite">
      <p class="dish__kicker">You know exactly what to do.</p>
      <p class="dish__text dish__text--turn">But she barely told you anything.</p>

      <button type="button" class="dish__turn" data-unsaid>
        What&rsquo;s missing? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </button>

      <!-- ========================================================
           THE UNSPOKEN DECISIONS — one click, then everything below
           plays out on its own. The five questions arrive one at a
           time, plain text and nothing else: no cards, no bubbles, no
           icons, just what actually went through your head on the
           way out the door. Once the last one has had a moment to be
           read, the realisation settles in beneath them — still no
           click between them, because nothing here is a further
           decision, only a beat settling. Nothing recedes: the point
           is a visitor reading down and connecting the instruction,
           every question it left open and the realisation as one
           composition.

           Nested one level inside the block it replaces, so the
           existing hand-over rule (kicker, turn line and button hide
           once [data-unsaid='1']) can reach them by the same technique
           every other beat in this story uses.
           ======================================================== -->
      <div class="dish__unsaid">
        <ul class="dish__asks">
          <li class="dish__ask" data-ask="1">Which shop?</li>
          <li class="dish__ask" data-ask="2">Where is everything?</li>
          <li class="dish__ask" data-ask="3">What if something is sold out?</li>
          <li class="dish__ask" data-ask="4">Are the tomatoes good?</li>
          <li class="dish__ask" data-ask="5">How do you pay?</li>
        </ul>

        <!-- The line the whole beat has been walking toward. Serif,
             full room, nothing after it yet — the AI-stack reveal is
             a separate, unbuilt beat. -->
        <p class="dish__realize">
          She gave you a goal.<br />
          You figured out the rest.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  /* =========================================================
     THE COLUMN
     One measure for the whole story, centred, so every beat hands over
     the same space instead of the page growing a new section each time.
     ========================================================= */
  .dish {
    padding: clamp(40px, 7vh, 86px) 0 clamp(72px, 12vh, 132px);
  }

  .dish__stage {
    max-width: 640px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* =========================================================
     SCENE 1
     ========================================================= */

  /* The scene, at the column's own measure. The painted content reaches
     the bottom edge of the 3:2 canvas, so there is nothing to trim off the
     box and the gap below is simply the gap to the line — the same
     relationship the homepage Feature has between its artwork and the
     sentence under it. */
  .dish__art {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0 auto;
    /* Quiets once the unspoken decisions open (see [data-unsaid='1']
       below) — same duration and easing the homepage Feature's own
       artwork uses for the equivalent moment, so the two places this
       picture appears settle the same way. */
    transition: opacity 900ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.72, 0.28, 1);
  }

  /* Present, not gone — quieted so it stops asking to be read while the
     realisation takes over, the same restrained treatment used wherever
     else this story's art needs to step back without disappearing. */
  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__art {
    opacity: 0.32;
  }

  /* The instruction, at the size of something said out loud. Serif,
     because this is the sentence the whole story hangs on — the same
     role the opening line has in every other story here. */
  .dish__quote {
    margin: clamp(18px, 2.6vh, 26px) 0 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.14;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* =========================================================
     THE SHARED VOICES
     Three roles, and the site's own three treatments for them: cobalt
     small caps-weight for the line that turns the thought, the page's
     sans for what helps you understand, and the serif for the sentence
     worth carrying away.
     ========================================================= */
  .dish__kicker {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--cobalt);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .dish__text {
    margin: 6px auto 0;
    max-width: 36ch;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* The turn in Scene 2 is the whole scene, so it gets the weight of a
     statement rather than of a supporting line. */
  .dish__text--turn {
    margin-top: 10px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(17px, 1.9vw, 20px);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  /* The way onward: the page-turn treatment the other stories use —
     serif, ink, a small saffron circle carrying the arrow. */
  .dish__turn {
    display: inline-block;
    margin: clamp(20px, 3vh, 28px) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: none;
    background: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.008em;
    cursor: pointer;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .dish__turn span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    margin-left: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--saffron);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 11px;
    vertical-align: middle;
    transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease;
  }

  .dish__turn:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .dish__turn:hover span {
    transform: scale(1.08);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(232, 117, 36, 0.35);
  }

  .dish__turn:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--cobalt);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @keyframes dish-in {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      translate: 0 8px;
    }
  }

  /* =========================================================
     SCENE 2 — the contradiction
     ========================================================= */
  .dish__wait {
    display: none;
    margin-top: clamp(30px, 4.5vh, 48px);
    padding-top: clamp(26px, 3.6vh, 36px);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
  }

  [data-stage='2'] .dish__wait {
    display: block;
    animation: dish-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 120ms;
  }

  /* The second half of the contradiction lands after the first has been
     read, not with it. */
  [data-stage='2'] .dish__text--turn {
    animation: dish-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 760ms;
  }

  [data-stage='2'] .dish__wait > .dish__turn {
    animation: dish-in 520ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 1500ms;
  }

  /* =========================================================
     SCENE 2b — the unspoken decisions
     The hand-over every story here uses: at [data-unsaid='1'] the kicker,
     turn line and their button leave the flow entirely, and the block
     below takes the space. Nested one level down on purpose, so this rule
     — which only reaches DIRECT children of .dish__wait — cannot hide it.
     ========================================================= */
  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__wait > .dish__kicker,
  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__wait > .dish__text--turn,
  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__wait > .dish__turn {
    display: none;
  }

  .dish__unsaid {
    display: none;
  }

  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__unsaid {
    display: block;
  }

  .dish__asks {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  /* Each question is its own beat, arriving one after another rather than
     as a block — the point is not the list, it is watching it keep going
     after you thought it had stopped. No base opacity here on purpose:
     .dish__unsaid is display:none until the scene opens, and
     animation-fill-mode: both already holds each question at the
     keyframe's opacity 0 through its own delay, the same technique the
     rest of this story uses. */
  .dish__ask {
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 32ch;
    padding: 7px 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: clamp(15.5px, 1.7vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__ask {
    animation: dish-in 460ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
  }

  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__ask[data-ask='1'] { animation-delay: 150ms; }
  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__ask[data-ask='2'] { animation-delay: 700ms; }
  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__ask[data-ask='3'] { animation-delay: 1250ms; }
  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__ask[data-ask='4'] { animation-delay: 1800ms; }
  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__ask[data-ask='5'] { animation-delay: 2350ms; }

  /* The realisation. Full serif weight and real room around it — the
     line the whole beat has been walking toward, not another supporting
     thought. Arrives once the last question has had a moment to be read,
     and stays alongside them: nothing here recedes, so the visitor can
     see the instruction, every question it left open and the realisation
     as one connected composition. */
  .dish__realize {
    margin: clamp(28px, 4.2vh, 44px) auto 0;
    max-width: 22ch;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3.1vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.026em;
  }

  [data-unsaid='1'] .dish__realize {
    animation: dish-in 700ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.78, 0.24, 1) both;
    animation-delay: 3100ms;
  }

  /* =========================================================
     REDUCED MOTION
     Nothing here communicates by movement — the sequencing communicates
     by ORDER, which survives when the animation does not. Every beat
     simply becomes visible in place, still in the same order, still one
     click at a time.
     ========================================================= */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .dish__wait,
    .dish__text--turn,
    .dish__turn,
    .dish__text,
    .dish__ask,
    .dish__realize {
      animation: none !important;
    }

    .dish__turn span,
    .dish__art {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .dish {
      padding-top: clamp(28px, 5vh, 48px);
    }

    .dish__quote {
      font-size: clamp(26px, 7.6vw, 34px);
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // One flag, set once. Everything "What's missing? →" opens — the
  // artwork quieting, the five questions, their recede, the realisation —
  // hangs off [data-unsaid='1'] in CSS; the script only sets it. There is
  // no further click inside this beat, so there is nothing else to gate:
  // it plays out on its own once started, the same way the rest of this
  // story's timed reveals do.
  //
  // Nothing here navigates, loads or reads anything outside this
  // component, and there is no analytics: this story is not registered
  // and story_complete is not defined, because the visitor has not
  // reached SEE DIFFERENTLY. The AI-stack reveal that follows this
  // realisation is a separate, unbuilt beat — this handler does not
  // anticipate it.
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-dish]').forEach((root) => {
    if (!(root instanceof HTMLElement)) return;

    const unsaid = root.querySelector('[data-unsaid]');
    if (!(unsaid instanceof HTMLElement)) return;

    unsaid.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (root.dataset.stage !== '2' || root.dataset.unsaid === '1') return;
      root.dataset.unsaid = '1';
    });
  });
</script>
